  $ codereach --no-e2e                   plaintext, for an existing pairing or if encryption is too slow
  $ codereach --e2e-auto-accept          pair the first phone without typing its code (terminal only;
                                           ${SHOW_PAIRING_PIPE_ENV}=1 also allows a pipe or log)
  $ codereach devices list               phones paired end to end
  $ codereach devices revoke <id>        stop trusting a phone
  $ codereach voice                      voice models installed on this computer
  $ codereach voice setup                choose and download a voice model
  $ codereach voice setup --language en  English, about 541 MB
  $ codereach upgrade                    update this copy to the latest release

OpenCode always listens on 127.0.0.1. No ports are opened on your network.

The end-to-end pairing QR and link are shown only when stdout is a terminal.
Set ${SHOW_PAIRING_PIPE_ENV}=1 to show them in a pipe or log too (whoever
